ild picks up the change. Someone should check that the release job runs from the new main.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the failing test.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ReHTgVb89Px653YVDRAVjJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018izKqtQdNwufdozMhweJFf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expects ROUND_HALF_EVEN, and the docstring already says so, but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. With HALF_EVEN, 2.675 \u2192 2.68 (7 is odd, so it rounds up to the even 8) and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 (6 is already even), which matches the test. I'll make that one-line change on a new branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TvUr8xXD1X56NsFtNpH3zu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01G85utYj4ZHFxLjan4TaC1s", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-banker-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money used ROUND_HALF_UP despite its docstring and FIN-212\nrequiring banker's rounding. This made tests/test_money.py fail on\n2.665 (expected 2.66, got 2.67).", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\